From 89c1858642887128fb12cbb28013b9a766dc6245 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:31:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] state: online stale-FTS recovery that needs neither an
 exclusive store nor a readable old index [daveey]

Hub, 2026-11-18: the trigram index of state.db had pages referenced twice, so DROP, 'delete-all'
and 'rebuild' all raised "database disk image is malformed". The one-shot rebuild also defers
while any other process holds the file, and supervised services always do ("futile"). Search
stayed on the LIKE fallback for hours; only a whole-store recovery with every holder stopped
could fix it.

hermes_state_fts_online:
- recover_stale_fts_online(): one short transaction drops the FTS triggers and source views,
  unlinks every messages_fts* table from sqlite_master (writable_schema; old pages are never
  read and stay allocated, reported by integrity_check as "never used", which
  integrity_damage_is_structural ignores), recreates both indexes with the shipping DDL, claims
  the chunked backfill and clears fts_stale. Under the rebuild admission lock; refused on a
  read-only or quarantined handle and on the legacy inline layout.
- advance_fts_backfill(): fts_rebuild_step chunks for a bounded time, chunk sized to the 0.25 s
  target; re-probes the trigram table so a handle never advances past rows it left out.
- retry_deferred_fts_recovery: adopts a peer's recovery (never redoes the one-shot over it), and
  takes the online path once the deferral is futile or the one-shot failed with a DB error.
- gateway: "FTS backfill tick" housekeeping chore. CLI: `hermes sessions repair-search
  [--force] [--wait]`. Futile-deferral log line and doctor name the new remedy.

Rehearsed on a copy of the hub's damaged store (12.6 GB, 1.35M messages): unlink 0.01 s,
backfill 13 min in 2,702 chunks, canonical tables hash-identical, both FTS integrity-checks ok,
search works, integrity_check reports only never-used pages.

Tests: tests/hermes_state/test_fts_online_recovery.py (page-level damaged trigram b-tree that
DROP cannot clear; peer writer adopting and interleaving; futile holder window; tick budget;
refusals; script scope; CLI; gateway tick).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
